=== W12: Health-scheduler integration ===
G0: control.rs guard_write() blocks invalid operations when paused/frozen; authority.rs require() checks role-based authority on every mutating path; breakglass::guard_effect blocks privileged operations below floor.

G1: cit/mod.rs execute() marks affected tasks retest_required=true and affected tests stale after material mutations (lines 924-967). Index refreshed after mutation.

G2: tasks.rs close() enforces input/consumption/traceability before task close: tests.status, work_completed, mutation scope violations, index freshness, governance currency (lines 386-563).

G3: handoffs.rs create() triggers before_handoff checkpoint (lines 94-107); checkpoints.rs stores context_packet_hash and memory_snapshot binding mandatory-input state across handoff.

G4: cit/mod.rs simulate() runs wider impact traversal after CIT proposals affecting spec/decision/architecture changes; estimate_radius() escalates radius for cross-feature/cross-module changes.

G5: verification/mod.rs audit() runs full governance suite across all families (schema, graph, freshness, retrieval regression, authority, mutation, secrets, context, claims, adapters, skills, commands, traceability, policy).

G6: Not implemented for artifact-flow-specific hidden faults in qualification. The advanced-qualification challenge describes the injection methodology (line 1194 of Contract v3), but the product does not yet inject hidden artifact-flow failures - that is Phase 4.

PRESENT_AND_SUBSTANTIAL: G0-G5 bullets executably evidenced. G6 is Phase 4 scope (hidden fault injection in qualification) - noted but not a Phase 2 blocker.
